WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.467
-I'm so happy to see you.
-I'm so happy to see you.

00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:03.834
I can't wait to get
into this movie

00:00:03.834 --> 00:00:05.567
'cause, gosh,
you're phenomenal in it.

00:00:05.567 --> 00:00:07.934
And I don't know how much
I can say about it,

00:00:07.934 --> 00:00:09.634
but, whatever,
let's get into it.

00:00:09.634 --> 00:00:12.734
First of all, was it last night
you just were at MoMA?

00:00:12.734 --> 00:00:14.901
You got honored.
-It was last night, yes.

00:00:14.901 --> 00:00:17.400
I'm still processing
the whole thing.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.667
It was really emotional,
really intense.

00:00:19.667 --> 00:00:20.868
I'm very grateful.

00:00:20.868 --> 00:00:23.501
-I mean, look at how gorgeous,

00:00:23.501 --> 00:00:26.267
by the way, last night
at this film benefit.

00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:27.767
Look at that, come on.

00:00:27.767 --> 00:00:29.567
Gorgeous.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:29.567 --> 00:00:30.767
For all the work
that you've done

00:00:30.767 --> 00:00:32.901
and then you get to see
kind of a retrospective.

00:00:32.901 --> 00:00:33.968
But you're just so young.

00:00:33.968 --> 00:00:35.634
I mean, it's interesting
you get this.

00:00:35.634 --> 00:00:37.334
-I mean, I feel young.

00:00:37.334 --> 00:00:41.667
And I was kind of...really
grateful but overwhelmed

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:45.167
and asking myself, "Why me?"

00:00:45.167 --> 00:00:46.834
-Well, you've done great things,
amazing stuff.

00:00:46.834 --> 00:00:49.000
And it was a great group of
people as well last night.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:51.901
-Yeah. Very grateful to all of
the people that came to support.

00:00:51.901 --> 00:00:53.067
-Yeah, it's wild.

00:00:53.067 --> 00:00:55.934
-People that I admire a lot
and that I love.

00:00:55.934 --> 00:00:58.767
-I know you're based
out of Madrid, right?

00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:00.501
-Yeah.
-But you lived in New York

00:01:00.501 --> 00:01:02.701
for a while when you first
started, right? Is that true?

00:01:02.701 --> 00:01:06.367
-I came here to study English
when I was around 19.

00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:09.634
And I spent a couple of years
but always going back and forth.

00:01:09.634 --> 00:01:13.501
And, yeah, it was a dream also

00:01:13.501 --> 00:01:15.267
to be able to work
in this industry.

00:01:15.267 --> 00:01:17.701
You know, I've been very lucky
to be able to work in

00:01:17.701 --> 00:01:20.234
a lot of different countries
in Europe and also here.

00:01:20.234 --> 00:01:22.734
-Yeah.
-Very lucky to have that.

00:01:22.734 --> 00:01:24.234
-And now here you are
back in New York.

00:01:24.234 --> 00:01:25.868
You're getting honored
in New York City.

00:01:25.868 --> 00:01:28.501
-If somebody would have told me
that when I was 19,

00:01:28.501 --> 00:01:29.968
I would be like, "No way."

00:01:29.968 --> 00:01:32.667
-I wanted to ask you because I
know -- I've seen clips

00:01:32.667 --> 00:01:36.501
of you and your husband being
pulled on stage at concerts.

00:01:36.501 --> 00:01:37.868
I don't know if it was
the Garden, maybe,

00:01:37.868 --> 00:01:39.167
that's what I'm thinking of
or maybe it was L.A.

00:01:39.167 --> 00:01:42.067
But U2?
-It happened with U2.

00:01:42.067 --> 00:01:44.000
It happened with Prince.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:45.834
-People just like to pull you
on stage and sing to you.

00:01:45.834 --> 00:01:47.934
-Apparently, yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.934 --> 00:01:49.801
-I mean, do you know

00:01:49.801 --> 00:01:51.367
that's going to happen
in advance or no?

00:01:51.367 --> 00:01:53.434
-With Bono, yes. He told us.

00:01:53.434 --> 00:01:55.200
And he said, "Come on.
You cannot say no."

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:59.300
We're very close friends
with him and the whole band.

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:01.300
But with Prince,
it was a surprise.

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:04.000
And I was very excited
to be there.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.634
But at the same time
I could not wait

00:02:05.634 --> 00:02:07.734
to get out of the sta--
the stage.

00:02:07.734 --> 00:02:09.267
It was terrifying.

00:02:09.267 --> 00:02:12.167
-Because you're --
Were you standing next to him?

00:02:12.167 --> 00:02:15.567
-Because he was expecting us --
expecting us to dance

00:02:15.567 --> 00:02:18.300
and maybe even sing
and it was terrifying.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:19.868
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:02:19.868 --> 00:02:21.100
Because you have nothing
planned.

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:22.968
You're like, "What do I do?"
-No, exactly.

00:02:22.968 --> 00:02:25.367
-Like, "I'm here to see you."
-Exactly.

00:02:25.367 --> 00:02:28.901
-I once remember doing a bit
with Bono and the band.

00:02:28.901 --> 00:02:30.834
He wanted me to come up
and do this thing,

00:02:30.834 --> 00:02:32.300
but he forgot to bring me up.

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:34.200
-No, he cannot do that to you!

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:36.000
-No, so I'm standing there --
-Next tour.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.667
-I'm like, "Hey, we rehearsed
this whole thing."

00:02:38.667 --> 00:02:40.400
And he just totally forgot
all about me.

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:43.033
I go, "Hey, buddy!"
Like, "I thought we had a bit."

00:02:43.033 --> 00:02:45.267
-Next tour, you have to be there
for sure.

00:02:45.267 --> 00:02:47.934
And he made us wear wigs
and all kinds of things.

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:49.300
-Yes, that's right!
That's what I saw.

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:51.334
Yeah, there was, like, a boa.
-But we loved it.

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:52.634
We love him so much.
-Oh, yeah.

00:02:52.634 --> 00:02:54.634
But I mean, you got to be
friends with Prince, right,

00:02:54.634 --> 00:02:55.868
after that, or...?

00:02:55.868 --> 00:02:58.200
-Actually, you know,

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:01.934
I kind of was like friends
with him at the beginning.

00:03:01.934 --> 00:03:03.434
It was weird because,
first of all,

00:03:03.434 --> 00:03:05.767
I said, "How should I call you?

00:03:05.767 --> 00:03:07.334
Symbol? Prince?"
Like, anything is weird.

00:03:07.334 --> 00:03:09.200
-Oh, yeah, he was a symbol
at one point.

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:10.334
Yeah, at point,
yeah, you're right.

00:03:10.334 --> 00:03:11.734
-But he was really kind to me

00:03:11.734 --> 00:03:13.200
and all my friends and family.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:15.400
And he used to throw these
parties at his house

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:17.601
that I'm sure you know about.
-I've read about, yeah.

00:03:17.601 --> 00:03:19.367
-And you probably have been
in some of them.

00:03:19.367 --> 00:03:21.000
-Unfortunately, no.
He forgot about me as well.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.934
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.934 --> 00:03:24.033
It happens, yeah.

00:03:24.033 --> 00:03:25.267
But I heard these parties

00:03:25.267 --> 00:03:27.801
start at like 1:00
in the morning and go all night.

00:03:27.801 --> 00:03:29.300
-Those parties were the parties.

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:31.033
I mean, I'm not very much
a party person.

00:03:31.033 --> 00:03:34.868
But when I went to those,
I would stay there until 5:00

00:03:34.868 --> 00:03:38.467
because the amazing things
that were happening

00:03:38.467 --> 00:03:39.767
in that living room.

00:03:39.767 --> 00:03:43.767
You could see Stevie Wonder
singing with Alicia Keys.

00:03:43.767 --> 00:03:47.868
And Farrell dancing with Diddy
and with Justin Timberlake.

00:03:47.868 --> 00:03:51.901
And I mean -- and then Prince
would join and play for a while

00:03:51.901 --> 00:03:53.300
and then he would
put the pajamas

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:54.734
and come back
and say good night

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:57.067
and he would go to bed
and leave all of us there.

00:03:57.067 --> 00:03:59.200
-He would come down in pajamas
and go, "I'm going to bed"?

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:00.667
-Once he did that --

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:02.701
came back with his pajamas
and say good night.

00:04:02.701 --> 00:04:04.701
-He said, "Lock up.
I'm going to sleep"?

00:04:04.701 --> 00:04:07.334
-No, he would leave everybody
at his house, partying.

00:04:07.334 --> 00:04:09.200
And he would go
or go into the studio

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:11.000
at that time of the night.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:13.000
But he was so kind and so sweet.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:15.400
And there is not one day
that I don't miss him.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:16.968
-Aww.

00:04:16.968 --> 00:04:20.234
I want to talk to you about your
new movie, "Parallel Mothers."

00:04:20.234 --> 00:04:21.601
You are so good in this.
-Thank you.

00:04:21.601 --> 00:04:24.834
-In fact, you -- It debuted at
Venice Film Festival.

00:04:24.834 --> 00:04:27.267
You got this --
You won this amazing award.

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:28.767
This is the -- Is it the Volpi?

00:04:28.767 --> 00:04:30.501
-The Volpi, yes.
-The Volpi Cup.

00:04:30.501 --> 00:04:32.334
-Yes.
-Can you explain what that is?

00:04:32.334 --> 00:04:35.667
-Well, that's the acting prize
in Venice.

00:04:35.667 --> 00:04:37.300
-In Venice.
-And it was such a big deal

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:40.400
for me because the first time
I went to the festival,

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:43.734
it was like 30 years ago, and I
went there with my first film.

00:04:43.734 --> 00:04:46.367
And then to win with a movie
with Pedro

00:04:46.367 --> 00:04:48.968
was really, really magical.

00:04:48.968 --> 00:04:50.701
Yeah.
-Yeah. That's a wild thing.

00:04:50.701 --> 00:04:52.000
Congratulations on this.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:53.567
I want to talk more about
the film when we come back.

00:04:53.567 --> 00:04:55.300
More with Penelope Cruz
after the break.

